le are the contract; do NOT modify them.\n\n## Required Changes\n\nAll seven files are new — use the **Write** tool for each (no `old_string`).\n\n### Change #1: package.json\n**File:** `services/frontend/package.json`\n**Action:** Write (new file). Exact version pins (no carets) for build\nreliability. The `start` script binds `0.0.0.0:3000` so the container port is\nreachable through the compose `3000:3000` mapping.\n**Content:**\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"frontend\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"next dev\",\n    \"build\": \"next build\",\n    \"start\": \"next start -H 0.0.0.0 -p 3000\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"next\": \"14.2.15\",\n    \"react\": \"18.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"18.3.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"typescript\": \"5.4.5\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"20.14.10\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"18.3.3\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"18.3.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Change #2: tsconfig.json\n**File:** `services/frontend/tsconfig.json`\n**Action:** Write (new file). Standard create-next-app TypeScript config;\n`architecture.yaml` names this exact path as the quality gate, so it must exist.\n**Content:**\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2017\",\n    \"lib\": [\"dom\", \"dom.iterable\", \"esnext\"],\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"module\": \"esnext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"preserve\",\n    \"incremental\": true,\n    \"plugins\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"next\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\"./*\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"next-env.d.ts\", \"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\", \".next/types/**/*.ts\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"node_modules\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Change #3: next.config.js\n**File:** `services/frontend/next.config.js`\n**Action:** Write (new file). Empty config object.\n**Content:**\n```js\n/** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */\nconst nextConfig = {};\n\nmodule.exports = nextConfig;\n```\n\n### Change #4: Root layout\n**File:** `services/frontend/app/layout.tsx`\n**Action:** Write (new file). The App Router refuses to build without a root\nlayout that renders `<html>`/`<body>`. It must contain **no `<h1>`** — the test\nlocator `page.locator('h1')` must resolve to exactly one element.\n**Content:**\n```tsx\nimport type { ReactNode } from 'react';\n\nexport const metadata = {\n  title: 'Frontend',\n};\n\nexport default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <body>{children}</body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Change #5: Home page\n**File:** `services/frontend/app/page.tsx`\n**Action:** Write (new file). Renders the single `<h1>`. Exact casing —\n`Hello world` (capital `H`, lowercase `w`); `toHaveText` is an exact match.\n**Content:**\n```tsx\nexport default function Home() {\n  return <h1>Hello world</h1>;\n}\n```\n\n### Change #6: Dockerfile\n**File:** `services/frontend/Dockerfile`\n**Action:** Write (new file). `libc6-compat` is the standard Next-on-Alpine SWC\nrequirement. Copy `package.json` alone before `npm install` (do NOT use a\n`package-lock.json*` wildcard — a wildcard COPY matching nothing fails the\nbuild, and no lockfile is shipped). `npm install` (not `npm ci`) installs\ndevDependencies too, which `next build` needs for the TypeScript check.\n**Content:**\n```dockerfile\nFROM node:20-alpine\nRUN apk add --no-cache libc6-compat\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package.json ./\nRUN npm install\nCOPY . .\nRUN npm run build\nEXPOSE 3000\nCMD [\"npm\", \"run\", \"start\"]\n```\n\n### Change #7: .dockerignore\n**File:** `services/frontend/.dockerignore`\n**Action:** Write (new file). Keeps host build artifacts out of the image.\n**Content:**\n```\nnode_modules\n.next\n```\n\n## Notes for the applier\n- All seven files are new